# The keys of a Hammerspoon theme file, each pointing at a role from theme/VOCABULARY. The
# left hand names are the eight colour roles Olm draws with, the kit's own words rather than
# anything Hammerspoon defines, and they are the only colours a plugin, a pane, a host or a
# component may name. See "Olm colour, eight roles and nothing else" in
# .hammerspoon/AGENTS.md.
#
# foreground is the ink, subtext is the ink stepped back, background is the fill of every
# panel, and border is the outline and divider colour, which the palette calls dim. highlight
# is the bar under the list cursor, the tint behind selected text and the fill of a key chip.
# primary, secondary and tertiary are the three accents, taken in order by graph series, and
# they carry rank rather than meaning, the same choice the vocabulary makes.
foreground = foreground
subtext    = subtext
background = background
border     = dim
highlight  = highlight
primary    = primary
secondary  = secondary
tertiary   = tertiary
